---
system: sys-12-support-admin-operations
flow_id: device-transfer-w4
surface: admin
spec_anchor: /software/systems/12-support-admin-operations#w4-device-transfer
actors: [AdminConsole, DeviceTransferService, PostgreSQL, MQTT, Device, AuditLog]
apis:
  - POST /admin/devices/:id/transfer
externals: [MQTT]
queues: []
failure_paths:
  - device_not_found
  - device_not_bound
  - transfer_already_pending
  - transaction_rollback
  - mqtt_publish_failure
idempotency: pending transfer guard — only one active transfer per device; transfer_code unique
retry: admin must wait 72h expiry or cancel existing transfer before retrying
timeout: 10s p99
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED. W4 from spec §4 — generates 6-char dictation-safe transfer code with 72h TTL.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant AdminConsole
    participant DeviceTransferService
    participant PostgreSQL
    participant MQTT
    participant Device
    participant AuditLog

    AdminConsole->>DeviceTransferService: POST /admin/devices/:id/transfer {reason}
    DeviceTransferService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT d.id, current_household_id FROM devices WHERE serial_number=$1

    alt device_not_found
        DeviceTransferService-->>AdminConsole: 404 device_not_found
    else device_not_bound
        Note over DeviceTransferService: current_household_id IS NULL
        DeviceTransferService-->>AdminConsole: 409 device_not_bound
    else has owner
        DeviceTransferService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT id FROM device_transfer_log WHERE device_id=$1 AND status='pending' AND transfer_code_expires_at > now()
        alt transfer_already_pending
            PostgreSQL-->>DeviceTransferService: existing pending row
            DeviceTransferService-->>AdminConsole: 409 transfer_already_pending
        else no pending
            DeviceTransferService->>DeviceTransferService: generate 6-char code from ABCDEFGHJKMNPQRSTUVWXYZ23456789 — expires_at = now() + 72h
            DeviceTransferService->>PostgreSQL: BEGIN
            alt transaction_rollback
                DeviceTransferService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE devices SET current_household_id=NULL, lifecycle_state='transfer_pending'
                DeviceTransferService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE device_ownership_history SET ended_at=now(), ownership_status='transferred'
                DeviceTransferService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT device_transfer_log (transfer_code, expires_at, initiated_by_admin_id, status='pending', reason)
                PostgreSQL-->>DeviceTransferService: error on any step
                DeviceTransferService->>PostgreSQL: ROLLBACK
                DeviceTransferService-->>AdminConsole: 500 transaction_rollback
            else committed
                DeviceTransferService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE devices ... COMMIT
                DeviceTransferService->>AuditLog: append {action: initiate_transfer, target: device, reason}
                alt mqtt_publish_failure
                    DeviceTransferService->>MQTT: publish tjbot/{deviceId}/commands/prepare-transfer {transfer_code, command_id, issued_by} (QoS 1, retained)
                    MQTT-->>DeviceTransferService: error
                    Note over DeviceTransferService,AdminConsole: transfer row already committed — MQTT retry on next admin poll
                    DeviceTransferService-->>AdminConsole: 502 mqtt_publish_failure {transferCode, expiresAt, requires_retry: true}
                else published
                    MQTT->>Device: deliver prepare_transfer command
                    Device->>Device: enter transfer mode (LED pattern + audio cue)
                    DeviceTransferService-->>AdminConsole: 200 {transferCode, expiresAt, fromHouseholdId}
                end
            end
        end
    end

    Note over AdminConsole,AuditLog: transfer code dictated by phone (excludes 0/O/1/I/L) — 72h TTL — code consumed by sys-02 consumer-provisioning
